  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given,</p><p>The angle of elevation of the top of a tower from a point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> due north of it is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> and from a point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> at a distance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn></math>&nbsp;units due west of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>cos</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>13</mn></msqrt></mfrac></mfenced></math>. If the distance of the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> from the tower is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn></math> units, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cot</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></math>&nbsp;is equal to</p><p>Now making the diagram of given value we have,</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/7abfce0b-98b5-4ca5-8ff3-fb510d75c6b0-image.png\" style=\"width: 338px; height: 250px;\" /></p><p>Given&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>13</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>tan</mi><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Now using the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>tan</mi><mi>&#946;</mi></math>&nbsp;in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#9651;</mo><mi>O</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;we get,&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/eaed5e41-ca93-4dd2-8def-f6805c72817f-551fbe22-619f-4236-9ac6-64ddc31cbca3-image.png\" style=\"width: 213px; height: 129px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>tan</mi><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>h</mi><mn>15</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>h</mi><mn>15</mn></mfrac></math>, so&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></math></p><p>Now in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#9651;</mo><mi>O</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/0632d039-1a94-4d71-9b56-7d372f9dd109-image.png\" style=\"width: 222px; height: 135px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>A</mi><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>225</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>O</mi><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>81</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>225</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>O</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></math></p><p>Now in triangle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#9651;</mo><mi>O</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi></math></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/9103f87a-a646-4462-a79c-7b31da804210-image.png\" style=\"width: 219px; height: 130px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>tan</mi><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>10</mn><mn>12</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>cot</mi><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>12</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math></p></blockquote>",
